<title>BELGIUM: Belgian 3rd beet test shows 7.93 tonnes sugar/ha.</title>
<headline>Belgian 3rd beet test shows 7.93 tonnes sugar/ha.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The third Belgian beet test for 1996 showed a sugar yield of 7.93 tonnes per hectare compared with 7.91 tonnes in the third test of 1995, said the Royal Belgian Institute for Improvement of Sugarbeet (IRAB).  </p>
<p>Details of third test versus year-ago result -</p>
<p>		    Root	 Sugar     Sugar   Leaf</p>
<p>		    weight     content   weight  weight</p>
<p>		    tns/ha	pct	tns/ha  tns/ha</p>
<p> 1996 (1)	 58.801     13.49     7.935   52.301</p>
<p> 1995 (1)	 52.820     14.98     7.914   36.251</p>
<p> 1986-95 (2)    56.060     14.85     8.328   53.363</p>
<p>Note - (1) Weighted mean (2) Arithmetic mean.</p>
<p>The third and final test was carried out on September 2.</p>
</text>
